diff --git a/docs/Reference/Server.md b/docs/Reference/Server.md
index 8832ddfc..175e651d 100644
--- a/docs/Reference/Server.md
+++ b/docs/Reference/Server.md
@@ -569,11 +569,33 @@ const fastify = require('fastify')({
       [require('ajv-keywords'), 'instanceof']
       // Usage: [plugin, pluginOptions] - Plugin with options
       // Usage: plugin - Plugin without options
-    ]
+    ],
+    onCreate: (ajvInstance) => {
+      // Called with the Ajv instance once it has been created and the
+      // `plugins` above have been applied, to further customize it
+      ajvInstance.addFormat('myFormat', (data) => typeof data === 'string')
+    },
+    mode: 'JTD' // Optional, switches the compiler to JSON Type Definition mode
   }
 })
 ```
 
+The whole object is forwarded, as is, to
+[`@fastify/ajv-compiler`](https://github.com/fastify/ajv-compiler#options):
+
++ `customOptions`: the [Ajv options](https://ajv.js.org/options.html) used to
+  build the instance. When `mode` is `'JTD'`, the
+  [Ajv JTD options](https://ajv.js.org/json-type-definition.html) are used
+  instead.
++ `plugins`: the [Ajv plugins](https://ajv.js.org/packages/) to apply. Every
+  plugin must return the Ajv instance it receives, as required by the
+  [Ajv plugin definition](https://ajv.js.org/packages/#ajv-plugins).
++ `onCreate`: a function called with the newly created Ajv instance, useful to
+  add keywords, formats, or schemas that cannot be set through options.
++ `mode`: set it to `'JTD'` to compile
+  [JSON Type Definition](https://ajv.js.org/json-type-definition.html) schemas
+  instead of JSON Schema ones.
+
 ### `serializerOpts`
 <a id="serializer-opts"></a>
 
